# G074 — Card Collector

*v2. See `card-collector.md` for prose: catalogue + collection bifurcation,
condition-weighted value, trade evaluation with tolerance, set difference
for "what's missing from my collection."*

---

## Choreographic Case: Vault Card Binder

[card-binder @catalogue-path @collection-path
    IN ORDER TO
        show current collection value and missing cards
        evaluate proposed trades within a tolerance

    @cat <- [cc[catalogue-load  {path: @catalogue-path}]]
    @col <- [cc[collection-load {path: @collection-path}]]

    #stats
        total-value: [cc[total-value {collection: @col, catalogue: @cat}]]
        unique:      [cc[unique-cards {collection: @col}]]
        missing:     [cc[missing {collection: @col, catalogue: @cat}]]

    sync @trade-proposals (@offered @asked) ->
        @result <- [cc[evaluate-trade
                        {offered: @offered, asked: @asked,
                         catalogue: @cat, tolerance-cents: 100}]]
        [ui[render-trade-verdict {result: @result}]]
]

---

## Verb Surface

[cc
    catalogue
    catalogue-add        {cat, card}
    catalogue-load       {path}
    collection
    collection-load      {path}
    add                  {col, card-id, condition, qty}
    remove               {col, card-id, condition, qty}   ;; || insufficient
    total-value          {col, cat}
    unique-cards         {col}
    missing              {col, cat}
    trade-bundle
    bundle-add           {bundle, card-id, condition, qty}
    evaluate-trade       {offered, asked, cat, tolerance}
]

---

## Distinctive Innate idiom: trade evaluation as `where`-judged verdict

[cc[evaluate-trade {offered: @o, asked: @a, cat: @c, tolerance: @t}
    where
        the offered bundle's value and the asked bundle's value
            are each computed via total-value
        and the trade is "fair" if |offered-value - asked-value| ≤ tolerance
        and the trade is "gives-up-value" if offered-value > asked-value + tolerance
        and the trade is "gains-value" if asked-value > offered-value + tolerance
    so verdict is a bare-word string the UI renders without judgment
]

---

## Demo

[demo
    @cat <- [cc[catalogue]]
    [cc[catalogue-add {cat: @cat,
                        card: {id: "A001", name: "Common", rarity: "common",
                               prices: {mint: 100, played: 40}}}]]
    [cc[catalogue-add {cat: @cat,
                        card: {id: "A002", name: "Rare", rarity: "rare",
                               prices: {mint: 5000, played: 2000}}}]]

    @col <- [cc[collection]]
    [cc[add {col: @col, card-id: "A001", condition: "mint", qty: 3}]]

    -> [cc[total-value {col: @col, cat: @cat}]]   ;; -> 300

    @offered <- [cc[trade-bundle]]
    [cc[bundle-add {bundle: @offered, card-id: "A001",
                     condition: "mint", qty: 3}]]
    @asked <- [cc[trade-bundle]]
    [cc[bundle-add {bundle: @asked, card-id: "A002",
                     condition: "played", qty: 1}]]

    -> [cc[evaluate-trade {offered: @offered, asked: @asked,
                            cat: @cat, tolerance-cents: 100}]]
    ;; -> {verdict: "gains-value", offered-value: 300, asked-value: 2000, delta: 1700}
]
